 Locate;Find
⍝ Make sure that DeltaWI.Locate can find names wherever they are in a sample GUI structure

⍝ Test structure:
⍝   MDIForm
⍝       Menu
⍝           Menu
⍝       Form
⍝           Menu
⍝               Menu
⍝           Label
⍝           Picture
⍝               Label
⍝? Later add checks using 'links', including those with relative references
⍝? 'links' are the only reasonable way to check for relative references within ∇Locate,
⍝? because most such naming constructions are handled by ∇ObjectName before they ever get to ∇Locate.

 '#'∆WI Pass MT⊢'Reset' ⍝ Clean out any previous GUI work

 ⍝ Build our main testing structure
 'mdi'∆WI Pass'mdi'⊢'New' 'MDIForm'
 'mdi.m1'∆WI Pass'mdi.m1'⊢'New' 'Menu'
 'mdi.m1.m2'∆WI Pass'mdi.m1.m2'⊢'New' 'Menu'
 'mdi.f'∆WI Pass'mdi.f'⊢'New' 'Form'
 'mdi.f.m1'∆WI Pass'mdi.f.m1'⊢'New' 'Menu'
 'mdi.f.m1.m2'∆WI Pass'mdi.f.m1.m2'⊢'New' 'Menu'
 'mdi.f.l'∆WI Pass'mdi.f.l'⊢'New' 'Label'
 'mdi.f.p'∆WI Pass'mdi.f.p'⊢'New' 'Picture'
⍝ 'mdi.f.p.l'∆WI Pass'mdi.f.p.l'⊢'New' 'Label' ⍝? Not yet available for testing

 ⍝ Now let's try to see if we can find specific object names
 Find←(∆WI Pass{×≢⍵})∘'self' ⍝ Give us a simple name to do the same thing over and over
 Find'mdi'
 Find'mdi.m1'
 Find'mdi.m1.m2'
 Find'mdi.f'
 Find'mdi.f.m1'
 Find'mdi.f.m1.m2'
 Find'mdi.f.l'
 Find'mdi.f.p'

 '#'∆WI Pass MT⊢'Reset' ⍝ Clean up after tests
